# /tests/fixtures/crasher, boot-fault role — fixture for a service that dies before its
# bootstrap request.
#
# Recipe lives under /config/svcmgr/tests/, which svcmgr does NOT scan.
# Co-staged with svctest in CI and stageable by hand: copy this file into
# /config/svcmgr/services/ between `cargo xtask build` and `cargo xtask
# run`. See docs/testing.md.
#
# An instance that finds the token /data/crasher-boot/die-early (its
# namespace's /die-early) removes it and faults before it asks svcmgr for its
# bootstrap round; any other instance serves ipc::restart_probe_labels on
# crasher.boot, as the worker-fault role does. The data partition ships the
# token, so the first launch dies so, and svctest's svcmgr_boot_death phase
# writes it again for a restart: svcmgr must route each such death under
# `restart = on_failure`, so a later instance answers the phase.
binary    = /tests/fixtures/crasher
argv      = crasher boot-fault
restart   = on_failure
critical  = no
namespace = subtree:/data/crasher-boot:LOOKUP+STAT+MUTATE_DIR
provides  = crasher.boot
